  "reason": "The existing evidence shows that multimodal models with multiprofile, scvi_n200 RNA encoder, and imagenet_vit_l image encoder (config_037) achieve the highest accuracy so far (0.706). This experiment tests whether replacing the RNA encoder with scgpt (a more advanced model) and using transformer aggregation (instead of avgpool) could further improve performance. It isolates the impact of the RNA encoder and aggregation method, which are critical design choices, while keeping the image encoder and fusion strategy consistent. This balances exploitation of the current top-performing setup with exploration of key variables."  
